1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
Grab the hundreds here, and the average guy loses two hundred grand.

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:08,172
Two piles of cash. Your weight in twenties, or your height in hundreds, stacked flat?

3
00:00:08,422 --> 00:00:11,047
Hundreds are worth five times more. Easy, right?

4
00:00:11,297 --> 00:00:12,826
Hit like if you picked the stack.

5
00:00:13,726 --> 00:00:17,674
But say a bill weighs about a gram. One pound is four hundred fifty-four bills.

6
00:00:17,924 --> 00:00:20,009
One inch of stack? Two hundred thirty-three.

7
00:00:20,309 --> 00:00:24,738
Average American man, per the CDC: one ninety-nine pounds, about five nine.

8
00:00:25,588 --> 00:00:28,762
Send this to the friend who'd grab the hundreds without— without blinking.

9
00:00:29,062 --> 00:00:33,476
His height in hundreds? One point six million. And that stack weighs thirty-five pounds.

10
00:00:33,776 --> 00:00:36,533
His weight's next. Follow, this page does the math you didn't.

11
00:00:36,983 --> 00:00:39,431
His weight in twenties: one point eight million.

12
00:00:40,981 --> 00:00:43,224
The small bills win, by two hundred grand.

13
00:00:43,524 --> 00:00:45,701
So… twenties or hundreds? One word.

